<!--
    kuna GH-180: "Overflow guards read the post-add value:
    v3 = v3 + v1; if (SCARRY8(v3,v1))"

    GNU grep -O2 nlscan (the in-repo witness tests/bug-repro/grep @ 0x7c90)
    guards a signed add against overflow:

        7ce0  4c 01 eb   add rbx,r13     ; OF := SCARRY8(rbx_pre, r13)
        7ce3  49 89 dd   mov r13,rbx
        7ce6  70 19      jo  7d01        ; tests OF from 7ce0

    kuna's IR keeps the SCARRY input (pre-add RBX) and the ADD output as two
    distinct Varnodes, but the two were merged into one HighVariable, so the
    emitted C read the guard AFTER the add on the same variable:

        v3 = v3 + v1;
        if (SCARRY8(v3,v1)) {            <- tests the post-add value

    a predicate the binary does not compute (Ghidra/IDA/Binja/angr all keep
    the operands pre-add).  Root cause: ActionMarkImplied set the implied flag
    directly instead of calling Merge::markImplied (upstream merge.cc:1595),
    which also marks every operand of the defining op coverdirty; and the
    Varnode coverdirty was not forwarded to the owning HighVariable the way
    upstream Varnode::setFlags does (varnode.cc:377-378).  With both halves
    missing, Cover::rebuild never re-ran after implied-marking, the operand
    Cover never grew to the CBRANCH where the implied SCARRY prints, and the
    cover-intersection test saw no conflict in the pre-add/post-add merge.

    Stage: P6 variable and storage model, explicit/implied marking + merge
    legality (docs/spec/06-variables-and-merge.md).  Correctness fix restoring
    upstream behavior, no option: single pass asserting the fixed shape.

    Function 1, `nlscan`: the verbatim witness bytes 0x7c90..0x7d05 with the
    trailing padding replaced by RET; `memchr` and the no-return error stub
    `die` are single-RET stand-ins at the real call targets.  Function 2,
    `grow`: the minimal unsigned form of the same idiom (the xalloc-style
    size-growth guard, grep @ 0x1f0d0 / gzip @ 0xf320):

        8000  48 8b 07     mov rax,[rdi]
        8003  48 89 c2     mov rdx,rax
        8006  48 d1 ea     shr rdx,1
        8009  48 83 c2 01  add rdx,0x1
        800d  48 01 d0     add rax,rdx   ; CF := CARRY8(rax_pre, rdx)
        8010  72 06        jb  8018      ; tests CF from 800d
        8012  48 89 07     mov [rdi],rax
        8015  31 c0        xor eax,eax
        8017  c3           ret
        8018  e8 43 fc ff ff  call die
        801d  c3           ret

    The asserts pin that each guard's operands are the PRE-add values: the
    intrinsic call must name the same tokens the sum expression adds, and the
    collapsed self-update-then-test rendering must not appear.
-->
